# R-SH11, R-NI16, R-SH1, R-SH5, R-LY3, R-CC6, R-HF1: share is not set, the registry is a URL, a person is there (tty, TALON_INTERACTIVE=1). The prompt comes before the work of the command (before the output of `cache dir`). The answer y writes share = true (the comment stays) and makes share.json (id, chmod 0600) under their locks. One tty call, and no answer line.
cache dir
# R-SH11: share is set now, so Talon does not ask again. The calls are the 2 reads of the first-run step and the command.
cache dir
# R-NI16, R-NM12, R-SH11, R-SH1: Enter is the default No: share = false is written (a new config.toml). No share.json. The prompt is the same.
env:HOME={w}/home/h2 cache dir
